# deployments/.env is gitignored and generated/appended to by several setup
# scripts (setup-aep.sh, seed-dev.sh, ...) — this file is NOT a complete
# template of every key they read, just the ones a developer is expected to
# set by hand. Copy what you need into deployments/.env.

# Required by scripts/setup-observability.sh's SRE-agent handoff wiring
# (HANDOFF_ENABLED=true, the default) — the long-lived Bearer credential the
# remediation agent's mounted mcp.json authenticates to aep-mcp-server with.
# Same credential the aectl/Helm path's aep-mcp-token ExternalSecret carries
# (OpenBao path aep/aep-mcp-token). See setup-observability.sh's header
# comment for AEP_MCP_HOSTNAME/AEP_MCP_TOKEN.
#
# aep-api (docker-compose) ALSO reads this exact value, as SRE_MCP_TOKEN —
# it's the side that actually verifies the Bearer aep-mcp-server presents.
# Set this BEFORE the first `docker compose up`/`start.sh`: a value added
# afterward needs aep-api recreated to take effect (setup-observability.sh
# does this for you automatically, but only when it next runs).
AEP_MCP_TOKEN=
